  "database": "rschema_0403",
  "nl_text": "The rschema_0403 database is a collection of six tables that store information about students, administrators, books, and the borrowing and returning of books. The tables are:\n1. Student: This table contains information about students, including their contact number, email, grade, major, name, student ID, and student number. The student ID is the primary key, and the student number is unique.\n2. Administrator: This table contains information about administrators, including their administrator ID, contact number, email, job number, name, and position. The administrator ID is the primary key.\n3. Book: This table contains information about books, including the author, book ID, borrowed quantity, category, publication date, publisher, stock quantity, and title. The book ID is the primary key.\n4. Student_Borrow_Book: This table contains information about the borrowing of books by students, including the borrow date, borrowed book ID, return date, review status, and student ID. The primary key is the combination of student ID and borrowed book ID.\n5. Student_Return_Book: This table contains information about the returning of books by students, including the book ID, return date, returned book ID, review status, and student ID. The primary key is the combination of student ID and returned book ID.\n6. Administrator_Audit: This table contains information about the auditing of books by administrators, including the administrator ID, audit date, audit result, book ID, borrowing status, and review status. The primary key is the combination of administrator ID and book ID.\nThe tables are related to each other through foreign keys, which ensure referential integrity and prevent orphaned records. For example, the Student_Borrow_Book and Student_Return_Book tables have foreign keys that reference the Book table, ensuring that the book IDs in those tables are valid. Similarly, the Administrator_Audit table has foreign keys that reference the Book and Student tables, ensuring that the book IDs and student IDs in that table are valid.",
  "gold_question": "Business Requirement Description:\nThe following describes a Library Management System. The system’s main features might include:\n1.Student Management: Includes adding, modifying, deleting, and querying student information. Each student has a Student ID, Name, Student Number, Grade, Major, Contact Number, and Email.\n2.Administrator Management: Includes adding, modifying, deleting, and querying administrator information. The administrator details include Administrator ID, Name, Job Number, Contact Number, Email, and Position.\n3.Book Management: Includes adding, modifying, deleting, and querying book information. Book details include Book ID, Title, Author, Publisher, Publication Date, Category, Stock Quantity, and Borrowed Quantity.\n4.Book Borrowing Management: Includes adding, modifying, deleting, and querying student borrowing records. The records include Student ID, Borrowed Book ID, Borrow Date, Return Date, and Review Status.\n5.Book Returning Management: Includes adding, modifying, deleting, and querying student returning records. The records include Student ID, Borrowed Book ID, Return Date, and Review Status.\n6.Audit Management: Administrators review book borrowing and returning actions. The audit includes Administrator ID, Book ID, Borrowing Status, Audit Date, and Audit Result.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0403.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0403\nCREATE TABLE `student` (\n  `student_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `student_number` varchar(50) NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_number` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `grade` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `major` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`student_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `administrator` (\n  `administrator_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_number` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `job_number` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `position` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`administrator_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `book` (\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `author` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `publisher` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `publication_date` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  `category` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stock_quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `borrowed_quantity` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`book_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `student_borrow_book` (\n  `student_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `borrowed_book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `borrow_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `return_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `review_status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`student_id`, `borrowed_book_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `student_borrow_book_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`student_id`) REFERENCES `student` (`student_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `student_borrow_book_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`borrowed_book_id`) REFERENCES `book` (`book_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `student_return_book` (\n  `student_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `returned_book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `return_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `review_status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`student_id`, `returned_book_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `student_return_book_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`student_id`) REFERENCES `student` (`student_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `student_return_book_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`returned_book_id`) REFERENCES `book` (`book_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `administrator_audit` (\n  `administrator_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `audit_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `audit_result` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `borrowing_status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `review_status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`administrator_id`, `book_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `administrator_audit_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`administrator_id`) REFERENCES `administrator` (`administrator_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `administrator_audit_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`book_id`) REFERENCES `book` (`book_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
